<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base down 2.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base down 2.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base fell 2.3 percent to 2.87 billion sucres ($776.5 million) in the week to March 21, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>The monetary base stood at 3.06 billion sucres at the end of 1996, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
